meta {
  name: Space Notify Repo Update
  type: http
  seq: 162
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.notifyRepoUpdate
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{serviceAuthToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main",
    "repo": "did:plc:memberaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
    "repoRev": "3kabcdefghij2",
    "data": { "$bytes": "BwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwcHBwc=" }
  }
}

docs {
  A repo host telling a space host that one of its repos advanced, so the authority can maintain
  the rev/hash listRepos reports. The space host then sends the update to every syncer
  registered through authorizeSpaceSync, as a repoWrite in notifySpaceUpdate. Carries no record
  data — just the new repoRev and commit hash (data). The forwarded form adds spaceRev and
  prevSpaceRev (omitted on the first update); a gap in prevSpaceRev means a missed
  notification, healed with listRepos and a spaceRev cursor.

  Authenticated with service auth (Authorization: Bearer <service-auth JWT>, lxm =
  com.atproto.space.notifyRepoUpdate, aud = this server's DID). Unlike uploadBlob's
  service-auth path, the issuer is deliberately NOT required to be a local account — a repo
  host is somewhere else by definition. It must be the repo whose head moved; anyone else is
  401.

  A notification about a space this server is not the authority for is accepted and dropped, as
  is one from a repo the space's write policy does not admit, and one whose repoRev does not
  advance the stored one (no writer-set change, nothing forwarded). Errors: 400 FutureRev when
  repoRev is more than five minutes ahead of this server's clock.
}
